        "original_id": "0675ebc9-1ed8-5786-9dd9-d86f0ca0fedf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Georges Favre, Paul Dukas, Vincent d'Indy\n- Roles: composer, musicologist, conductor, critic, scholar, teacher\n- Works: The Sorcerer's Apprentice\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Dukas was a French composer, critic, scholar, and teacher who lived from 1 October 1865 to 17 May 1935.\n- Paul Dukas is best known for the orchestral piece The Sorcerer's Apprentice (L'apprenti sorcier).\n- Georges Favre was a French composer and musicologist who lived from 26 July 1905 to 25 April 1993.\n- Georges Favre studied composition with Paul Dukas and conducting with Vincent d'Indy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
